                 "Outcome: The release conforms: the library checker found the library valid with this course in it, and pySHACL found all 287 documents it checks conform."@en .

<https://archive.org/details/SwedishCourseText>
    dcterms:title "Swedish Basic Course (Foreign Service Institute, 1982), student text as scanned on the Internet Archive (item \"Swedish Basic Course Text\")" ;
    dcterms:creator "Ingrid Beach, Anne-Marie Carnemark, Margareta Feller and Margareta Weyl, with the editorial assistance of Allen I. Weinstein; Foreign Service Institute, U.S. Department of State" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/> ;
    rdfs:comment "Checking: the Internet Archive's OCR text of the student text, searched for the course's grammar points and phrases on 18 November 2026 (quoted with OCR errors corrected). Unit 1: \"Most Swedish verbs in the present tense end in -r\", \"Notice that inte comes after the verb\", and Talar ni svenska? as a question with the verb first; Unit 2: the ending for the, -en and -et, and \"Mitt, ditt, vårt, ert – used with ett words\"; Unit 3: the five plural classes; Unit 4: ett stort glas and Rummet är stort; Unit 5: \"the verb comes in second place\"; Unit 8: ingen, inget and inga; Unit 10: the imperative; Unit 12: det var så lite among the answers to tack så mycket, and bjuda på. A work of the United States Government: the title page reads \"FOREIGN SERVICE INSTITUTE U.S. DEPARTMENT OF STATE 1982\", and the text carries no copyright notice. 17 U.S.C. § 105 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/17/105): \"Copyright protection under this title is not available for any work of the United States Government\". The Internet Archive item's metadata (https://archive.org/metadata/SwedishCourseText) gives creator \"Foreign Service Institute\" and licenseurl \"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/\". Recorded here with the Public Domain Mark: free of known copyright. Chapters 3 to 9 were checked against it in the same way: Unit 1 (helping verbs), Unit 2 (ska and kommer att, the time), Units 3 and 5 (the past tense, the supine, tänker, som, sin), Unit 9 (comparison), Units 7 and 9 (den stora boken), Unit 10 (reflexive verbs, inte in a subordinate clause, hade with the supine), Unit 11 (hälsa på, tack för senast, tack för maten), Unit 13 (tycka, tänka, tro), Unit 14 (allemansrätten) and Unit 15 (Lucia, julafton, the maypole). What the course takes from it is checking of grammar points and meanings, not its text."@en .

<https://www.wikidata.org/>
