<https://en.wiktionary.org/>
    dcterms:title "English Wiktionary (Swedish entries)" ;
    dcterms:creator "Wiktionary contributors" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/> ;
    rdfs:comment "Verification only; no text was taken from it. 36 key words of the fronts and notes were looked up on 18 November 2026: 33 have a Swedish entry, and the genders and definitions read agree with the course (påtår a second cup of coffee, pant a container deposit, våning a floor, kvar left or remaining, mittemot opposite, gärna gladly, bjuda with på to offer, lås a lock, ludd lint, behövas the passive of behöva, fika common gender with neuter as an alternative); vad får det lov att vara? is an entry (what will it be?, when taking an order). tvättid, kardemummabulle (which has since left the course) and barista have no Swedish entry. For chapters 3 to 9, 45 more words were looked up the same day: 42 have a Swedish entry that agrees with the course (hen, a gender-neutral pronoun; bruka, auxiliary, to use to; tänka, to intend; lagom, just right; glögg, alcoholic or not; lussekatt, a saffron bun; semla, eaten on Shrove Tuesday; midsommarafton, the Friday from 19 to 25 June); julfest and falurött have no page, and maja has no Swedish section. Text is available under CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Wiktionary:Copyrights)."@en .

# Chapter 0: The first fika.

<#ch-fika>
