# Chapter 2: The laundry room.

<#ch-laundry>
    a solid-memo:Chapter ,
      schema:Syllabus ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <> ;
    schema:position 2 ;
    dcterms:title "The laundry room"@en ,
                  "Tvättstugan"@sv ,
                  "Die Waschküche"@de ,
                  "La lavandería"@es ,
                  "La buanderie"@fr ,
                  "세탁실"@ko ;
    dcterms:description "Sam meets Elin in the building's shared laundry room: booking a time, whose things are whose, a pink sheet, and asking a neighbor politely to make way. Ends with a review of the chapter."@en ,
                        "Sam träffar Elin i husets gemensamma tvättstuga: boka en tid, vems saker som är vems, ett rosa lakan och att be en granne snällt att göra plats. Avslutas med en repetition av kapitlet."@sv ,
                        "Sam trifft Elin in der gemeinsamen Waschküche des Hauses: eine Zeit buchen, was wem gehört, ein rosa Laken und einen Nachbarn höflich bitten, Platz zu machen. Endet mit einer Wiederholung des Kapitels."@de ,
                        "Sam se encuentra con Elin en la lavandería común del edificio: reservar un turno, de quién es cada cosa, una sábana rosa y pedirle con cortesía a un vecino que deje sitio. Termina con un repaso del capítulo."@es ,
                        "Sam retrouve Elin dans la buanderie commune de l'immeuble : réserver un créneau, savoir à qui sont les affaires, un drap devenu rose et demander poliment à un voisin de laisser la place. Se termine par une révision du chapitre."@fr ,
                        "샘은 건물의 공용 세탁실에서 엘린을 만납니다. 시간 예약하기, 어느 물건이 누구 것인지, 분홍색으로 물든 시트, 이웃에게 정중하게 자리를 비켜 달라고 부탁하기를 다룹니다. 챕터 복습으로 끝납니다."@ko ;
    solid-memo:reviewQuestion <#q-laundry-r01> ,
                              <#q-laundry-r02> .

<#ch-laundry-1>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-laundry> ;
    schema:position 0 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Booking a time

*A Wednesday evening in September. Sam takes a bag of laundry down to the building's laundry room, where Elin is folding towels.*

**Sam:** Hej! Är maskinerna lediga?\\
*Hi! Are the machines free?*

**Elin:** Nej, tyvärr. Jag har tvättid till nio.\\
*No, sorry. I have the laundry room until nine.*

**Sam:** Tvättid? Måste man boka?\\
*A laundry slot? Do you have to book?*

**Elin:** Ja, man bokar på tavlan vid dörren. Sätt ditt lås på den tiden du vill ha.\\
*Yes, you book on the board by the door. Put your lock on the time you want.*

**Sam:** Okej. Var är torktumlaren?\\
*OK. Where's the dryer?*

**Elin:** Den står bredvid torkskåpet. Och glöm inte att städa efter dig!\\
*It's next to the drying cabinet. And don't forget to clean up after yourself!*

---

**Är maskinerna lediga?**: "Are the machines free?" *Ledig* is free or vacant; it also means off work: *Jag är ledig i morgon*.

**Tvättid**: a booked time in the laundry room. Most apartment buildings in Sweden share one, and its times are booked, often on a board with a lock of your own, a booking cylinder, or on a screen.

**Måste man …?**: "Does one have to …?", "Do you have to …?" *Måste* is must; the verb after it has no *-r*: *boka*.

**Sätt! Glöm inte!**: an order or request drops the ending of the present tense: *-r* after an *a* (*kollar → kolla*, *tvättar → tvätta*), otherwise *-er* (*sätter → sätt*; *glömmer → glöm*, with one *m*, as Swedish words seldom end in *-mm*). Short verbs just drop the *-r*: *går → gå*, *bor → bo*. *Glöm inte att …* is "Don't forget to …".

**Städa efter dig**: "Clean up after yourself": wipe the machines and empty the lint filter. The next person in line will notice if you don't."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-laundry-0a> ,
                         <#q-laundry-0b> ,
                         <#q-laundry-0c> .

<#q-laundry-0a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-11-18T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "Är maskinerna lediga?"@sv ;
    solid-memo:back "Are the machines free?"@en ,
                    "Sind die Maschinen frei?"@de ,
                    "¿Están libres las máquinas?"@es ,
                    "Est-ce que les machines sont libres ?"@fr ,
                    "기계들 비어 있나요?"@ko ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Asked of a neighbor in a shared laundry room. Maskinerna is the machines, plural with the ending for the; ledig is free or vacant."@en ,
                        "Fragt man einen Nachbarn in der gemeinsamen Waschküche. Maskinerna heißt die Maschinen, Plural mit der Endung für den bestimmten Artikel; ledig heißt frei oder unbesetzt."@de ,
                        "Se le pregunta a un vecino en una lavandería común. Maskinerna es las máquinas, en plural con la terminación del artículo definido; ledig es libre o desocupado."@es ,
                        "Se demande à un voisin dans une buanderie commune. Maskinerna veut dire les machines, au pluriel avec la terminaison de l'article défini ; ledig veut dire libre ou disponible."@fr ,
                        "공용 세탁실에서 이웃에게 묻는 말이에요. Maskinerna는 '그 기계들'로, 정관사 어미가 붙은 복수예요. ledig는 비어 있다, 쓸 수 있다는 뜻이에요."@ko ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-laundry-0a-d1> ,
                          <#q-laundry-0a-d2> ,
                          <#q-laundry-0a-d3> .

