<#ch-weekend-2>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-weekend> ;
    schema:position 1 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## How it works: the past tense

*Monday morning at work. Johan meets Sam at the coffee machine.*

**Johan:** Hej Sam! Vad gjorde du i helgen?\\
*Hi Sam! What did you do over the weekend?*

**Sam:** I lördags var jag i skogen med min granne Elin. Vi plockade kantareller.\\
*Last Saturday I was in the woods with my neighbor Elin. We picked chanterelles.*

**Johan:** Vad kul! Hittade ni många?\\
*How fun! Did you find a lot?*

**Sam:** En hel korg! På kvällen stekte vi dem i smör. Och du?\\
*A whole basket! In the evening we fried them in butter. And you?*

**Johan:** Jag var hemma och städade. Det regnade hela söndagen.\\
*I was at home cleaning. It rained all day Sunday.*

**Sam:** Stackars dig!\\
*Poor you!*

---

**The past tense** (*preteritum*) is the same for every person, like the present: *jag var, du var, vi var*. Verbs fall into four groups by how they make it:

- **-ar → -ade**: *plockar → plockade*, *städar → städade*, *regnar → regnade*, *hittar → hittade*. Most verbs are like this.
- **-er → -de or -te**: *ringer → ringde*; after *k, p, s* or *t*, *-te*: *köper → köpte*, *steker → stekte*.
- **Short verbs, -r → -dde**: *bor → bodde*, *tror → trodde*.
- **Strong and irregular verbs**, to learn one by one: most change their vowel and take no ending, *äter → åt*, *tar → tog*, *finns → fanns*; some are irregular, *går → gick*, *är → var*, *gör → gjorde*.

**Time phrases**: *i lördags* is last Saturday, *på lördag* next Saturday; *förra veckan* is last week. *I helgen* can be the weekend just gone or the one coming: the tense tells which (*Vad gjorde du i helgen?*, *Vad ska du göra i helgen?*).

**The verb still comes second** when a time comes first: *I lördags var jag i skogen*, *På kvällen stekte vi dem*.

**Var hemma och städade**: "was at home cleaning". Swedish often says what someone was doing with *och* and a second verb in the same tense."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-weekend-1a> ,
                         <#q-weekend-1b> ,
                         <#q-weekend-1c> .

<#q-weekend-1a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-11-18T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "Vad gjorde du i helgen?"@sv ;
    solid-memo:back "What did you do over the weekend?"@en ,
                    "Was hast du am Wochenende gemacht?"@de ,
                    "¿Qué hiciste el fin de semana?"@es ,
                    "Qu'est-ce que tu as fait ce week-end ?"@fr ,
                    "주말에 뭘 했어요?"@ko ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Asked by a colleague on Monday morning, the usual small talk at work. Gjorde is the past tense of göra (do), so i helgen is the weekend just gone."@en ,
                        "Fragt ein Kollege am Montagmorgen, der übliche Smalltalk bei der Arbeit. Gjorde ist das Präteritum von göra (machen), also ist i helgen das gerade vergangene Wochenende."@de ,
                        "Lo pregunta un compañero el lunes por la mañana, la charla de siempre en el trabajo. Gjorde es el pasado de göra (hacer), así que i helgen es el fin de semana que acaba de pasar."@es ,
                        "Demandé par un collègue le lundi matin, la conversation habituelle au travail. Gjorde est le passé de göra (faire), donc i helgen désigne le week-end qui vient de passer."@fr ,
                        "월요일 아침에 동료가 묻는 말로, 직장에서 흔히 하는 가벼운 대화예요. Gjorde는 göra(하다)의 과거형이라서 i helgen은 막 지나간 주말이에요."@ko ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-weekend-1a-d1> ,
                          <#q-weekend-1a-d2> ,
                          <#q-weekend-1a-d3> .

<#q-weekend-1a-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "What are you doing this weekend?"@en ,
                              "Was machst du dieses Wochenende?"@de ,
                              "¿Qué vas a hacer este fin de semana?"@es ,
                              "Qu'est-ce que tu vas faire ce week-end ?"@fr ,
                              "이번 주말에 뭐 할 거예요?"@ko ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be Vad ska du göra i helgen?; gjorde is the past tense of göra."@en ,
                              "Das wäre Vad ska du göra i helgen?; gjorde ist das Präteritum von göra."@de ,
                              "Eso sería Vad ska du göra i helgen?; gjorde es el pasado de göra."@es ,
                              "Ce serait Vad ska du göra i helgen? ; gjorde est le passé de göra."@fr ,
                              "그 뜻이라면: Vad ska du göra i helgen?; gjorde는 göra의 과거형이에요."@ko .

