# Chapter 8: Planning midsummer.

<#ch-plan>
    a solid-memo:Chapter ,
      schema:Syllabus ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <> ;
    schema:position 8 ;
    dcterms:title "Planning midsummer"@en ,
                  "Vi planerar midsommar"@sv ,
                  "Wir planen Mittsommer"@de ,
                  "Preparando Midsommar"@es ,
                  "Préparer la Saint-Jean"@fr ,
                  "하지 축제 계획"@ko ;
    dcterms:description "Sam, Elin and her friend Nora plan how to celebrate midsummer at Nora's family's summer house: who brings what, likes, guesses and plans, and settling things together. Ends with a review of the chapter."@en ,
                        "Sam, Elin och hennes vän Nora planerar hur de ska fira midsommar i Noras familjs sommarstuga: vem som tar med vad, vad man tycker om, tror och tänker göra och att bestämma saker tillsammans. Avslutas med en repetition av kapitlet."@sv ,
                        "Sam, Elin und ihre Freundin Nora planen, wie sie Mittsommer im Sommerhaus von Noras Familie feiern: wer was mitbringt, Vorlieben, Vermutungen und Pläne, und Dinge gemeinsam festmachen. Endet mit einer Wiederholung des Kapitels."@de ,
                        "Sam, Elin y su amiga Nora planean cómo celebrar Midsommar en la casa de veraneo de la familia de Nora: quién lleva qué, gustos, suposiciones y planes, y ponerse de acuerdo entre todos. Termina con un repaso del capítulo."@es ,
                        "Sam, Elin et Nora, une amie d'Elin, prévoient comment fêter la Saint-Jean dans la maison de campagne de la famille de Nora : qui apporte quoi, ce qu'on aime, ce qu'on suppose et ce qu'on compte faire, et se mettre d'accord ensemble. Se termine par une révision du chapitre."@fr ,
                        "샘, 엘린, 엘린의 친구 노라가 노라 가족의 여름 별장에서 하지 축제를 어떻게 보낼지 계획합니다. 누가 무엇을 가져올지, 좋아하는 것, 짐작과 계획, 함께 정하기를 다룹니다. 챕터 복습으로 끝납니다."@ko ;
    solid-memo:reviewQuestion <#q-plan-r01> ,
                              <#q-plan-r02> .

<#ch-plan-1>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-plan> ;
    schema:position 0 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Who brings what

*An evening in May. Elin has invited Sam and her friend Nora over to plan midsummer, which Nora's family celebrates at their summer house.*

**Elin:** Sam, det här är Nora. Vi har känt varandra sedan skolan.\\
*Sam, this is Nora. We've known each other since school.*

**Nora:** Hej Sam! Vill du fira midsommar med oss på landet?\\
*Hi Sam! Would you like to celebrate midsummer with us in the country?*

**Sam:** Gärna! Vad ska jag ta med?\\
*I'd love to! What shall I bring?*

**Nora:** Kan du ta med jordgubbar? Mamma fixar sill och potatis.\\
*Could you bring strawberries? Mom is taking care of the herring and potatoes.*

**Elin:** Och jag bakar en glutenfri jordgubbstårta.\\
*And I'll bake a gluten-free strawberry cake.*

**Sam:** Det låter bra! Hur blir vädret, tror ni?\\
*Sounds good! What will the weather be like, do you think?*

**Nora:** Det regnar nästan alltid på midsommar. Ta med regnkläder!\\
*It almost always rains at midsummer. Bring rain gear!*

**Elin:** Jag håller med. Men vi firar ändå!\\
*I agree. But we celebrate anyway!*

---

**Vi har känt varandra sedan skolan**: "We've known each other since school." *Känna* is to know a person; *veta* is to know a fact. *Varandra* is each other.

**På landet**: in the country, outside the towns. *Till landet* or *ut på landet* is to the country.

**Vad ska jag ta med?**: "What shall I bring?" At a Swedish party where everyone helps, guests often bring part of the food, and asking is expected.

**Mamma fixar …**: *fixa* is everyday Swedish for to sort out, take care of. *Mamma* without *min* is how Swedes speak of their own mother to friends.

**Det låter bra!**: "Sounds good!" *Låta* is to sound.

**Jag håller med**: "I agree." *Jag håller inte med* is "I don't agree"; *Jag håller med dig* is "I agree with you".

**Regn på midsommar**: rain at midsummer is a running Swedish joke. People plan for it and celebrate anyway."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-plan-0a> ,
                         <#q-plan-0b> ,
                         <#q-plan-0c> .

<#q-plan-0a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-11-18T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "Vill du fira midsommar med oss på landet?"@sv ;
    solid-memo:back "Would you like to celebrate midsummer with us in the country?"@en ,
                    "Möchtest du mit uns auf dem Land Mittsommer feiern?"@de ,
                    "¿Quieres celebrar Midsommar con nosotros en el campo?"@es ,
                    "Tu veux fêter la Saint-Jean avec nous à la campagne ?"@fr ,
                    "시골에서 우리랑 같이 하지 축제를 보낼래요?"@ko ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Asked by Nora, inviting Sam to her family's summer house. Vill du …? is a friendly invitation; på landet is in the countryside."@en ,
                        "Fragt Nora und lädt Sam ins Sommerhaus ihrer Familie ein. Vill du …? ist eine freundliche Einladung; på landet heißt auf dem Land."@de ,
                        "Lo pregunta Nora al invitar a Sam a la casa de veraneo de su familia. Vill du …? es una invitación amable; på landet es en el campo."@es ,
                        "Demandé par Nora, qui invite Sam dans la maison de campagne de sa famille. Vill du …? est une invitation amicale ; på landet veut dire à la campagne."@fr ,
                        "노라가 샘을 자기 가족의 여름 별장에 초대하며 묻는 말이에요. Vill du …?는 다정한 초대이고, på landet는 '시골에서'예요."@ko ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-plan-0a-d1> ,
                          <#q-plan-0a-d2> ,
                          <#q-plan-0a-d3> .

<#q-plan-0a-d1>
