                              "그 뜻이라면: Hon bor vid sjön, bredvid den gula stugan; som ligger vid sjön은 오두막이 어디에 있는지 말해요."@ko .

# Chapter 9: The first midsummer.

<#ch-midsummer>
    a solid-memo:Chapter ,
      schema:Syllabus ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <> ;
    schema:position 9 ;
    dcterms:title "The first midsummer"@en ,
                  "Första midsommaren"@sv ,
                  "Der erste Mittsommer"@de ,
                  "El primer Midsommar"@es ,
                  "La première Saint-Jean"@fr ,
                  "첫 하지 축제"@ko ;
    dcterms:description "Sam spends Midsummer Eve at Nora's family's summer house: raising the maypole, dancing Små grodorna, asking politely with skulle and saying what happens if, and a light night when Sam and Elin look back on the year. Ends with a review of the chapter."@en ,
                        "Sam firar midsommarafton i Noras familjs sommarstuga: resa midsommarstången, dansa Små grodorna, be artigt med skulle och säga vad som händer om, och en ljus natt då Sam och Elin ser tillbaka på året. Avslutas med en repetition av kapitlet."@sv ,
                        "Sam verbringt den Mittsommerabend im Sommerhaus von Noras Familie: die Mittsommerstange aufstellen, Små grodorna tanzen, höflich mit skulle bitten und sagen, was passiert, wenn …, und eine helle Nacht, in der Sam und Elin auf das Jahr zurückblicken. Endet mit einer Wiederholung des Kapitels."@de ,
                        "Sam pasa la víspera de Midsommar en la casa de veraneo de la familia de Nora: levantar el palo de mayo, bailar Små grodorna, pedir con cortesía con skulle y decir qué pasa si…, y una noche clara en la que Sam y Elin repasan el año. Termina con un repaso del capítulo."@es ,
                        "Sam passe la veille de la Saint-Jean dans la maison de campagne de la famille de Nora : dresser le mât, danser Små grodorna, demander poliment avec skulle et dire ce qui se passe si, et une nuit où il fait encore jour où Sam et Elin repensent à l'année. Se termine par une révision du chapitre."@fr ,
                        "샘은 노라 가족의 여름 별장에서 하지 전야를 보냅니다. 메이폴 세우기, Små grodorna 춤추기, skulle로 정중하게 부탁하기와 '만약 ~하면'을 말하기, 그리고 샘과 엘린이 한 해를 돌아보는 환한 밤을 다룹니다. 챕터 복습으로 끝납니다."@ko ;
    solid-memo:reviewQuestion <#q-midsummer-r01> ,
                              <#q-midsummer-r02> .

<#ch-midsummer-1>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-midsummer> ;
    schema:position 0 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Raising the maypole

*Midsummer Eve, a Friday in late June. Elin and Sam arrive at Nora's family's summer house by a lake, where the maypole lies on the grass, covered in leaves and flowers.*

**Nora:** Hej och välkomna! Glad midsommar!\\
*Hi and welcome! Happy midsummer!*

**Sam:** Glad midsommar! Vad fint det är här vid sjön.\\
*Happy midsummer! How lovely it is here by the lake.*

**Nora:** Ni kommer precis i tid.\\
*You're just in time.*

**Elin:** Varför då?\\
*How come?*

**Nora:** Vi ska resa midsommarstången nu. Ta tag i repet där borta, och alla drar på tre!\\
*We're going to raise the maypole now. Grab the rope over there, and everyone pulls on three!*

**Elin:** Ett, två, tre … Nu står den!\\
*One, two, three … Now it's standing!*

**Nora:** Kom, nu dansar vi Små grodorna.\\
*Come on, now we're dancing Små grodorna.*

**Sam:** Måste jag hoppa som en groda?\\
*Do I have to hop like a frog?*

**Elin:** Ja, alla hoppar. Barnen, Noras mormor och du också!\\
*Yes, everyone hops. The children, Nora's grandma and you too!*

---

**Glad midsommar!**: "Happy midsummer!", the greeting of the day, as *God jul* is at Christmas.

**Ni kommer precis i tid**: "You're just in time." *Ni* is *you* to more than one, Elin and Sam together; *precis i tid* is just in time (*precis* is exactly, *i tid* on time).

**Varför då?**: "How come?", "Why's that?" *Då* makes *varför* softer and more curious.

**Resa midsommarstången**: to raise the maypole. *Resa* here is to raise or put upright (*resa sig* is to stand up); the same verb also means to travel. The pole is also called *majstången*.

**Ta tag i …**: "grab hold of …". *Alla drar på tre*: everyone pulls on three, in the present tense for what happens next.

**Måste jag …?**: "Do I have to …?" *Måste* is followed by the verb without *-r*, as in *Måste man boka?* from the laundry room.

**Små grodorna** ("The little frogs") is the best-known of the songs danced around the maypole: the frogs have no ears and no tails, so the dancers hop like frogs and hold their hands to their ears and behind them. Children and grandparents dance together, and nobody is too old or too new to join in."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-midsummer-0a> ,
                         <#q-midsummer-0b> ,
                         <#q-midsummer-0c> .

<#q-midsummer-0a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-11-18T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "Ni kommer precis i tid."@sv ;
    solid-memo:back "You're just in time."@en ,
                    "Ihr kommt genau rechtzeitig."@de ,
                    "Llegáis justo a tiempo."@es ,
                    "Vous arrivez juste à temps."@fr ,
                    "두 사람 딱 맞춰 왔네요."@ko ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Said by Nora to Elin and Sam as they arrive at her summer house, just before the maypole goes up. Ni is you to more than one; precis i tid is just in time."@en ,
                        "Sagt Nora zu Elin und Sam, als die beiden an ihrem Sommerhaus ankommen, kurz bevor die Mittsommerstange aufgestellt wird. Ni ist ihr, also mehr als eine Person; precis i tid heißt genau rechtzeitig."@de ,
                        "Lo dice Nora a Elin y Sam cuando llegan a su casa de veraneo, justo antes de levantar el palo de mayo. Ni es tú para más de una persona, es decir vosotros; precis i tid es justo a tiempo."@es ,
                        "Dit par Nora à Elin et Sam qui arrivent à sa maison de campagne, juste avant qu'on dresse le mât. Ni veut dire vous, à plusieurs personnes ; precis i tid veut dire juste à temps."@fr ,
                        "메이폴을 세우기 직전, 여름 별장에 도착한 엘린과 샘에게 노라가 하는 말이에요. Ni는 둘 이상에게 쓰는 '너희'이고, precis i tid는 '딱 제시간에'예요."@ko ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-midsummer-0a-d1> ,
                          <#q-midsummer-0a-d2> ,
                          <#q-midsummer-0a-d3> .

