<#q-midsummer-1c>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-11-18T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "Om det regnar, äter vi jordgubbarna inne."@sv ;
    solid-memo:back "If it rains, we'll eat the strawberries inside."@en ,
                    "Falls es regnet, essen wir die Erdbeeren drinnen."@de ,
                    "Si llueve, nos comemos las fresas dentro."@es ,
                    "S'il pleut, on mangera les fraises à l'intérieur."@fr ,
                    "비가 오면 딸기는 안에서 먹어요."@ko ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Said by Nora, the host, at an outdoor midsummer dinner as clouds come in. Om with the present tense is a real possibility; after the om clause, the verb äter comes before vi."@en ,
                        "Sagt Nora als Gastgeberin bei einem Mittsommeressen im Freien, als Wolken aufziehen. Om mit dem Präsens ist eine echte Möglichkeit; nach dem om-Satz steht das Verb äter vor vi."@de ,
                        "Lo dice Nora, la anfitriona, en una cena de Midsommar al aire libre, cuando llegan las nubes. Om con el presente es una posibilidad real; después de la oración con om, el verbo äter va antes de vi."@es ,
                        "Dit par Nora, l'hôtesse, lors d'un dîner de la Saint-Jean en plein air, alors que les nuages arrivent. Om avec le présent exprime une possibilité réelle ; après la proposition en om, le verbe äter vient avant vi."@fr ,
                        "구름이 몰려올 때 야외 하지 축제 저녁 자리에서 주인인 노라가 하는 말이에요. 현재형과 함께 쓰는 Om은 실제로 일어날 수 있는 일이에요. om 절 뒤에서는 동사 äter가 vi 앞에 와요."@ko ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-midsummer-1c-d1> ,
                          <#q-midsummer-1c-d2> ,
                          <#q-midsummer-1c-d3> .

<#q-midsummer-1c-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "If it had rained, we would have eaten the strawberries inside."@en ,
                              "Wenn es geregnet hätte, hätten wir die Erdbeeren drinnen gegessen."@de ,
                              "Si hubiera llovido, nos habríamos comido las fresas dentro."@es ,
                              "S'il avait plu, on aurait mangé les fraises à l'intérieur."@fr ,
                              "비가 왔으면 딸기는 안에서 먹었을 거예요."@ko ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be Om det hade regnat, hade vi ätit jordgubbarna inne; regnar is the present tense, a real possibility now."@en ,
                              "Das wäre Om det hade regnat, hade vi ätit jordgubbarna inne; regnar ist Präsens, eine echte Möglichkeit jetzt."@de ,
                              "Eso sería Om det hade regnat, hade vi ätit jordgubbarna inne; regnar está en presente, una posibilidad real ahora."@es ,
                              "Ce serait Om det hade regnat, hade vi ätit jordgubbarna inne ; regnar est au présent, une possibilité réelle maintenant."@fr ,
                              "그 뜻이라면: Om det hade regnat, hade vi ätit jordgubbarna inne; regnar는 현재형으로, 지금 실제로 일어날 수 있는 일이에요."@ko .

<#q-midsummer-1c-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "It's raining, so we're eating the strawberries inside."@en ,
                              "Es regnet, also essen wir die Erdbeeren drinnen."@de ,
                              "Está lloviendo, así que nos comemos las fresas dentro."@es ,
                              "Il pleut, alors on mange les fraises à l'intérieur."@fr ,
                              "비가 오니까 딸기는 안에서 먹어요."@ko ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be Det regnar, så vi äter jordgubbarna inne; om is if, so it has not started raining."@en ,
                              "Das wäre Det regnar, så vi äter jordgubbarna inne; om heißt falls, also hat es noch nicht angefangen zu regnen."@de ,
                              "Eso sería Det regnar, så vi äter jordgubbarna inne; om es si, así que todavía no ha empezado a llover."@es ,
                              "Ce serait Det regnar, så vi äter jordgubbarna inne ; om veut dire si, il n'a donc pas encore commencé à pleuvoir."@fr ,
                              "그 뜻이라면: Det regnar, så vi äter jordgubbarna inne; om은 '만약'이라서 아직 비가 오기 시작하지 않았어요."@ko .

<#q-midsummer-1c-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "When it stops raining, we'll eat the strawberries outside."@en ,
                              "Wenn es aufhört zu regnen, essen wir die Erdbeeren draußen."@de ,
                              "Cuando deje de llover, nos comemos las fresas fuera."@es ,
                              "Quand il arrêtera de pleuvoir, on mangera les fraises dehors."@fr ,
                              "비가 그치면 딸기는 밖에서 먹어요."@ko ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be När det slutar regna, äter vi jordgubbarna ute; inne is inside."@en ,
                              "Das wäre När det slutar regna, äter vi jordgubbarna ute; inne heißt drinnen."@de ,
                              "Eso sería När det slutar regna, äter vi jordgubbarna ute; inne es dentro."@es ,
                              "Ce serait När det slutar regna, äter vi jordgubbarna ute ; inne veut dire à l'intérieur."@fr ,
                              "그 뜻이라면: När det slutar regna, äter vi jordgubbarna ute; inne는 '안에서'예요."@ko .

<#ch-midsummer-3>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-midsummer> ;
    schema:position 2 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Another way it goes: the light night

*Near midnight. The rain never came. Elin and Sam sit on the dock by the lake, and the sky is still pale.*

**Elin:** Klockan är nästan tolv, och det är fortfarande ljust.\\
*It's almost midnight, and it's still light.*

**Sam:** Minns du vår första fika? Jag kunde bara lite svenska då.\\
*Do you remember our first fika? I only knew a little Swedish then.*

**Elin:** Och i kväll har du pratat svenska hela tiden! Minns du ditt rosa lakan?\\
*And tonight you've been speaking Swedish the whole time! Do you remember your pink sheet?*

**Sam:** Det har jag fortfarande! Det har varit ett fantastiskt år. Tack för allt, Elin.\\
*I still have it! It's been a fantastic year. Thank you for everything, Elin.*

**Elin:** Själv tack. Glöm inte att lägga sju sorters blommor under kudden i natt!\\
*Thank you too. Don't forget to put seven kinds of flowers under your pillow tonight!*

**Sam:** Jag skulle inte vilja bo någon annanstans.\\
*I wouldn't want to live anywhere else.*

**Elin:** Välkommen hem, Sam. Skål!\\
*Welcome home, Sam. Cheers!*

---

**Minns du …?**: "Do you remember …?" *Minnas* ends in *-s* in every form: *jag minns*, *jag mindes*. *Komma ihåg* means the same. *Vår* is our (*vårt*, *våra*, as *min, mitt, mina*); it is also the word for spring.

**Det har varit**: "It has been", *har* and the supine, looking back on a time that reaches up to now.

**Själv tack**: "Thank you too", the answer when someone thanks you and you are just as grateful; the same as *Tack själv!*, which Lena said over the semlor.

**Jag skulle inte vilja …**: "I wouldn't want to …". *Inte* comes right after *skulle*, the first verb.

**Sju sorters blommor**: an old Midsummer custom: pick seven kinds of wild flowers, often in silence, and put them under your pillow, and you will dream of the one you are going to marry.

**The light night**: around midsummer the sun sets only for a few hours in Uppsala, and the sky never gets fully dark; in the far north the sun does not set at all.

**Midsummer Eve**, *midsommarafton*, is always a Friday between 19 and 25 June, and most people have the day off, though it is not an official public holiday. It is often the biggest party of the Swedish year: herring, new potatoes, strawberries, and drinking songs (*snapsvisor*) before the schnapps. At *Skål!* you look each other in the eye before and after you drink."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-midsummer-2a> ,
                         <#q-midsummer-2b> ,
                         <#q-midsummer-2c> .

<#q-midsummer-2a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-11-18T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "Minns du vår första fika?"@sv ;
    solid-memo:back "Do you remember our first fika?"@en ,
                    "Erinnerst du dich an unsere erste Fika?"@de ,
                    "¿Te acuerdas de nuestra primera fika?"@es ,
                    "Tu te souviens de notre première fika ?"@fr ,
                    "우리 첫 피카 기억나요?"@ko ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Asked by Sam of Elin on midsummer night, looking back on the year since they met. Minns is the present tense of minnas, to remember; vår is our."@en ,
                        "Fragt Sam Elin in der Mittsommernacht, im Rückblick auf das Jahr, seit die beiden sich kennengelernt haben. Minns ist das Präsens von minnas, sich erinnern; vår heißt unser."@de ,
                        "Se lo pregunta Sam a Elin en la noche de Midsommar, mirando atrás al año que ha pasado desde que se conocieron. Minns es el presente de minnas, recordar; vår es nuestra."@es ,
                        "Demandé par Sam à Elin la nuit de la Saint-Jean, en repensant à l'année écoulée depuis leur rencontre. Minns est le présent de minnas, se souvenir ; vår veut dire notre."@fr ,
                        "하지 축제 밤, 만난 지 1년을 돌아보며 샘이 엘린에게 묻는 말이에요. Minns는 minnas(기억하다)의 현재형이고, vår는 '우리의'예요."@ko ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-midsummer-2a-d1> ,
                          <#q-midsummer-2a-d2> ,
                          <#q-midsummer-2a-d3> .

<#q-midsummer-2a-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Do you remember your first fika?"@en ,
                              "Erinnerst du dich an deine erste Fika?"@de ,
                              "¿Te acuerdas de tu primera fika?"@es ,
                              "Tu te souviens de ta première fika ?"@fr ,
                              "엘린 씨의 첫 피카 기억나요?"@ko ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be Minns du din första fika?; vår is our, din is your."@en ,
                              "Das wäre Minns du din första fika?; vår heißt unser, din heißt dein."@de ,
                              "Eso sería Minns du din första fika?; vår es nuestra, y din, tu."@es ,
                              "Ce serait Minns du din första fika? ; vår veut dire notre, din ta."@fr ,
                              "그 뜻이라면: Minns du din första fika?; vår는 '우리의', din은 '너의'예요."@ko .

